  "full_response": "As a language model, I can't create physical shipping labels, but I can provide you with a template you can use to create one. Below is a sample format for a shipping label that includes placeholders for the necessary information.\n\n### Sender's Information\n- **Full Name:** John Doe\n- **Street Address:** 123 Maple Street\n- **City, State, ZIP Code:** Springfield, IL, 62704\n- **Phone Number:** (555) 123-4567\n- **Email Address:** johndoe@example.com\n\n### Recipient's Information\n- **Full Name:** Jane Smith\n- **Street Address:** 456 Oak Avenue\n- **City, State, ZIP Code:** Anytown, NY, 12345\n- **Phone Number:** (555) 987-6543\n- **Email Address:** janesmith@example.com\n\n### Package Information\n- **Description of Contents:** Books\n- **Tracking Number:** (To be added by carrier)\n\n### Instructions for Creating a Shipping Label\n1. **Use a Shipping Service:** Go to a shipping service provider like USPS, FedEx, UPS, or their respective websites.\n2. **Enter Shipping Details:** Input the sender's and recipient's information as shown in the template.\n3. **Pack the Item:** Ensure your package is well-sealed and ready for shipping.\n4. **Generate a Label:** Use the shipping service's online tool to generate a shipping label. Print it and attach it to your package.\n5. **Drop Off or Schedule Pickup:** Take your package to a shipping center or schedule a pickup as per the carrier's instructions.\n\nMake sure to double-check all information for accuracy before finalizing the shipping label.",
